---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../consts';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Why Open-Source Code Review — OpenReview"
	description="Why OpenReview is an open-source AI code review agent: bring your own API keys, customize your review rules, and self-host on your infrastructure."
>
	<section class="manifesto article-width container">
		<p class="eyebrow">The OpenReview manifesto</p>
		<h1>
			Open by nature.
			<br />
			Forward by design.
		</h1>
		<div class="prose">
			<p>
				Code review should move good work forward. It should be the moment an
				idea gets clearer, a teammate learns something new, and a team becomes a
				little more confident in what it ships.
			</p>
			<p>
				Too often, it becomes the opposite: another queue, another wall of
				notifications, another conversation without the context it needs.
			</p>
			<h2>Clarity is a feature.</h2>
			<p>
				We believe the best tools make room for the work. A diff should be easy
				to read. Feedback should stay close to the code. The next step should be
				obvious.
			</p>
			<h2>Conversations, not verdicts.</h2>
			<p>
				A review is a shared effort to make something better. We’re designing
				OpenReview around useful context, focused discussions, and clear
				resolutions—so feedback can turn into progress.
			</p>
			<h2>Your tools should belong to you.</h2>
			<p>
				OpenReview is open source because the people who use a tool should be
				able to understand it, question it, and improve it. Read the source.
				Open an issue. Help us decide what comes next. As an open-source AI code review agent, OpenReview lets you bring your own API keys, define your review rules in Markdown, and self-host on your own infrastructure.
			</p>
			<blockquote>
				<p>
					Good code is a team effort.
					<br />
					Good tools should be, too.
				</p>
			</blockquote>
		</div>
		<div class="identity-signature">
			<Logo markOnly />
			<span class="mono muted">
				OPEN SOURCE.
				<br />
				DEVELOPER DRIVEN.
			</span>
		</div>
		<a class="button" href={GITHUB_URL}>
			Build with us on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
		</a>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
